#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0012 expect=noViolation domain=BW
#note "Every variable the SENDIG declares Required for BW is present, the columns spelled in lower case as a SAS dataset may carry them. SEND12 tests presence: a present column in any letter case is present (column names match case-insensitively, owner ruling 2026-09-28; the rule compares the upper-cased dataset names against the library's upper-case names) -> conformant, no finding."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#library required-variables BW STUDYID DOMAIN USUBJID BWSEQ BWTESTCD
dataset BW label="Body Weight"
col studyid  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col domain   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col usubjid  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col bwseq    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col bwtestcd type=Char label="Body Weight Test Short Name"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | BW
